  "title": "India's Current Account Deficit Widens to $31.98 Billion Amid Economic Growth and Global Challenges",
  "summary": "India's current account deficit widened to $31.98 billion in Q1FY27, partially offset by growth in exports of petroleum products, electronics, engineering, and marine goods. The deficit is expected to continue growing as global economic conditions evolve.",
